<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Camp Windy Loop (via East Fork Trail/Windy Peak Traverse/Bonney Junction/Bennett Ridge Trail)</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:191-4: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.310224" lon="-121.641836"><ele>1426.3</ele><name>Bennett Pass Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:bennett-pass-sno-park, as in 190-1; confidence: high; pdf_page: 207; book_elev_ft: 4674; quote: This 0.8-mile trail connects Bennett Pass with Pocket Creek. Although marked at Bennett Pass the trailhead is not obvious.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.309802" lon="-121.628009"><ele>1315.5</ele><name>East Fork Trail west end (Tie Trail / Teacup Lake Trail clearcut)</name><desc>source: OSM node 33434179 on Forest Road 3540, 24 m from the end of the Pocket Creek - Bennet Pass Tie trail 682 (way 475739377); as in 202-5; confidence: high; pdf_page: 207; quote: It soon enters a large clearcut where a road is descended steeply to the East Fork Trail road and the Teacup Lake Trail junction.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.302220" lon="-121.603446"><ele>1288.4</ele><name>Upper Junction of Pocket Creek</name><desc>source: OSM junction of Forest Road 3540 and 3540-640, as in 202-5 and 206-1; confidence: high; pdf_page: 205; book_elev_ft: 4200; quote: The East Fork Trail's east end joins with the Meadows Creek, Pocket Creek, and upper Pocket Creek trails.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.295170" lon="-121.593280"><ele>1428.4</ele><name>Mount Adams view clearcut</name><desc>source: as in 206-1: OSM node 3713226242 on Forest Road 3540-640; confidence: high; pdf_page: 208; book_elev_ft: 4640; quote: from the Upper Junction ski upward 1.3 miles on the upper Pocket Creek road to the Mount Adams view clearcut at 4,640 feet</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.296500" lon="-121.590500"><ele>1491.4</ele><name>Top, northeast corner of the clearcut</name><desc>source: as in 206-1 (placed; clearcut edge not mapped); confidence: low; pdf_page: 208; quote: Climb to the top, northeast corner of the clearcut, enter forest, and zigzag upward</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.295000" lon="-121.583000"><ele>1744.6</ele><name>Saddle north of Windy Peak</name><desc>source: as in 206-1: DEM col north of Windy Peak (Point 5801), DEM 5,722 ft; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 208; quote: zigzag upward to the flat, forested saddle north of Windy Peak</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.293000" lon="-121.582300"><ele>1736.7</ele><name>East slope below the saddle</name><desc>source: as in 206-1 (placed); confidence: low; pdf_page: 193; quote: From Camp Windy climb generally open slopes to the broad saddle just north of Windy Peak (Point 5801)</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.291300" lon="-121.583000"><ele>1705.8</ele><name>Foot of the east slope</name><desc>source: as in 206-1 (placed); confidence: low; pdf_page: 208; quote: Another reward is the descent on open slopes to Camp Windy</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.289979" lon="-121.586767"><ele>1704.5</ele><name>Camp Windy</name><desc>source: as in 190-1: OSM node 3667973324, Camp Windy Trail #685B leaves Gunsight Trail #685; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 192; quote: Camp Windy is located 1 mile northeast of Bonney Junction at the head of Boulder Creek.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.286393" lon="-121.588045"><ele>1712.6</ele><name>Windy Point</name><desc>source: as in 190-1: OSM node 3669738830 on Gunsight Trail #685; confidence: low; pdf_page: 192; quote: ski north through forest on a scenic route to Windy Point, a shoulder with unusual rock formations</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.279104" lon="-121.596418"><ele>1632.9</ele><name>Bonney Junction</name><desc>source: as in 190-1: OSM node 3669713797 on Forest Road 3550; confidence: high; pdf_page: 191; book_elev_ft: 5360; quote: At Bonney Junction (5,360 feet), a forested saddle, roads lead to Camp Windy and Bonney Butte</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.298990" lon="-121.608880"><ele>1463.9</ele><name>Windy Saddle (west foot of the Terrible Traverse)</name><desc>source: as in 190-1: OSM node 5164478227 on Forest Road 3550; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 189; book_elev_ft: 4800; quote: the trail descends to Windy Saddle at the west foot of the Terrible Traverse</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.310224" lon="-121.641836"><ele>1426.3</ele><name>Bennett Pass Sno-Park (finish)</name><desc>source: as start; confidence: high; pdf_page: 188; book_elev_ft: 4674; quote: the return by way of Bonney Junction and the long downhill run to the Terrible Traverse</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Camp Windy Loop (via East Fork Trail/Windy Peak Traverse/Bonney Junction/Bennett Ridge Trail)</name><desc>1. Bennett Pass Sno-Park -&gt; East Fork Trail west end (Tie Trail / Teacup Lake Trail clearcut): osm (high), 0.93 mi | 2. East Fork Trail west end (Tie Trail / Teacup Lake Trail clearcut) -&gt; Upper Junction of Pocket Creek: osm (high), 1.61 mi | 3. Upper Junction of Pocket Creek -&gt; Mount Adams view clearcut: osm (high), 1.32 mi | 4. Mount Adams view clearcut -&gt; Top, northeast corner of the clearcut: straight (low), 0.16 mi | 5. Top, northeast corner of the clearcut -&gt; Saddle north of Windy Peak: straight (low), 0.38 mi | 6. Saddle north of Windy Peak -&gt; East slope below the saddle: straight (low), 0.14 mi | 7. East slope below the saddle -&gt; Foot of the east slope: straight (low), 0.12 mi | 8. Foot of the east slope -&gt; Camp Windy: straight (medium), 0.20 mi | 9. Camp Windy -&gt; Windy Point: osm (high), 0.26 mi | 10. Windy Point -&gt; Bonney Junction: osm (high), 0.69 mi | 11. Bonney Junction -&gt; Windy Saddle (west foot of the Terrible Traverse): osm (high), 1.78 mi | 12. Windy Saddle (west foot of the Terrible Traverse) -&gt; Bennett Pass Sno-Park (finish): osm (high), 2.24 mi</desc>
